**Given:**

Selling Price (SP) = ₹289

Loss Percentage (L) = 15%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP}{1 - (L)/(100)}

**Calculation:**

CP = dfrac{289}{1 - (15)/(100)}

⇒ CP = dfrac{289}{0.85}

⇒ CP = 340

**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**

